# Prettier owns JSON only, and `format:check` is a real gate because of it.
#
# Source is excluded because the code is written to a wider effective line length than any Prettier
# setting matches, and ESLint already enforces what matters; reformatting it would churn every file
# for no gain. Markdown is excluded because Prettier pads every table cell to the column width, so
# changing one word rewrites the whole table and every future documentation diff becomes unreadable.
# A gate that always warns is worse than no gate, so the scope is narrowed rather than the gate
# softened.
*.ts
*.tsx
*.js
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.css
*.html
*.md
# YAML too: Prettier rewrites Compose's double-quoted scalars to single quotes, and compose.yaml is
# a file people copy and edit against Docker's own documentation.
*.yaml
*.yml
